<del></del></span> Best Restoration Shaman Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>For Healer trinkets in Phase 1, there are only two that are from raiding and those are the ones we want the most. As getting two raid trinkets can be hard, you will likely have to run Celestial Dungeon Trinkets or Relic of Yu'lon.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is a great option and much cheaper than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a>, making it the ideal budget choice.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> can also be excellent for the whole of Phase 1 due to its extremely high Intellect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87163/spirits-of-the-sun">
<img alt="Spirits of the Sun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_29_sunkissedwine.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirits of the Sun</span></a> is the best raid trinket in Phase 1, providing a lot of Intellect and Spirit while being fully passive.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is a strong trinket for Restoration, as you can line its on use effect with your cooldowns while also spreading them to hit various incoming damage events every minute. It is also easy to get since all you need is Valor Points and some reputation with our best faction.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87075/qin-xis-polarizing-seal">
<img alt="Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal</span></a> is fairly decent, but because most of its value is in the Intellect proc, it will lead to spiky healing which can not line up with damage events you want to cooldown for.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> provides Spirit on use for a little bit of added Regen, which unfortunately does not multiply with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=16190/mana-tide-totem">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_summonwaterelemental.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mana Tide Totem</span></a>, making it a decent but not great option.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> is primarily a DPS trinket but can also be a decent trinket for Phase 1, especially if you can make use of its huge Haste bonus while using cooldowns.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87065/light-of-the-cosmos">
<img alt="Light of the Cosmos" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Light of the Cosmos</span></a> is another DPS-focused trinket and not quite as reliable as Essence of Terror since it will mostly proc off your <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=8050/flame-shock">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_flameshock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flame Shock</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
